+
+#### [LexNLP](https://github.com/LexPredict/lexpredict-lexnlp)
+> **Description:** LexNLP is one of the best-known open source libraries for information retrieval and extraction over real legal text. Its README focuses on contracts, policies, procedures, and other unstructured legal documents, with utilities for amounts, dates, definitions, citations, conditional language, and domain-specific parsing. Lawyers and legal engineers can use it as a component inside clause review tools, legal analytics pipelines, and contract ingestion workflows. The project is dual-licensed with AGPL-3.0 as the default open source option, and its long history makes it a practical foundation when legal-domain NLP matters more than generic text processing.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/LexPredict/lexpredict-lexnlp](https://github.com/LexPredict/lexpredict-lexnlp)
