+#### [Blackstone](https://github.com/ICLRandD/Blackstone)
+> **Description:** Blackstone is a spaCy pipeline and model tuned for unstructured legal text. The repository is aimed at caselaw and legal NLP, giving lawyers and research teams a domain-specific alternative to general-purpose named-entity models. In practice, that is useful when you need legal entities, procedural references, citations, and legal terminology to be recognized with fewer domain mismatches. The codebase is Python-first and easy to slot into downstream classification, summarization, and search systems. For legal AI builders who want a narrower, more lawyer-relevant NLP layer before passing text into an LLM, Blackstone is still one of the clearest GitHub options.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/ICLRandD/Blackstone](https://github.com/ICLRandD/Blackstone)
+- **Stars:** 674 ⭐
