+#### [LexGLUE](https://github.com/coastalcph/lex-glue)
+> **Description:** LexGLUE is a benchmark dataset suite for legal language understanding in English. It is not an end-user application, but it matters because law firms, legal AI startups, and academic teams need reproducible evaluation datasets before trusting any contract or case-law model in production. The repository is especially useful for testing document classification, multi-label prediction, and legal-domain model quality. If your team is comparing summarization, retrieval, or legal classification approaches, LexGLUE gives you a baseline rather than pure anecdotal testing. GitHub metadata shows a smaller but still meaningful research community around the project, and the repository remains relevant for legal model evaluation.
