+#### [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is one of the most capable open OCR stacks on GitHub for turning PDFs and images into structured data. Its repository description now explicitly frames the toolkit as a bridge between documents and LLMs, which is exactly the legal use case for scanned filings, exhibits, invoices, wet-signature forms, and legacy contracts. It supports 100+ languages, includes document parsing components, and is maintained at a pace that many narrower OCR libraries cannot match. For legal teams handling large archives of scanned PDFs, PaddleOCR is often the best first-choice engine when they need extraction quality, scale, and active development in a single public repository.
