+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for helping improve `awesome-best-ai-tools-for-lawyers-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+Every submission must include:
+
+1. A public GitHub repository URL in the form `https://github.com/owner/repo`
+2. A short note explaining why the tool is useful for lawyers, legal ops, compliance, e-discovery, contract review, privacy, or legal engineering
+3. The repository license as shown on GitHub
+4. The primary language, star count, and most recent update or commit date from GitHub
+5. A short description based on the project README, not marketing copy
+
+## What Will Be Rejected
+
+- Proprietary SaaS products with no public GitHub repository
+- Private or archived repositories with no practical maintenance path
+- Repositories that are only prompt collections with no usable software or dataset value
+- Duplicates of tools already listed
